.TH ag-policy-preset 1  "preset 0.3.0-beta.6"
.SH NAME
ag\-policy\-preset \- Ready\-made policies: solo, team, agents, strict
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag policy preset\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ready\-made policies: solo, team, agents, strict
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ag\-policy\-preset\-list(1)
List the presets and who each is for
.TP
ag\-policy\-preset\-show(1)
Print the policy document a preset makes, and what it means
.TP
ag\-policy\-preset\-apply(1)
Store a preset as the stream\*(Aqs next policy version (needs an admin)
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.6
